  "slug": "gland-development-mll4-4b67",
  "summary": "Single-cell and long-read multiomic data now allow regulatory links to be tested within individual samples and under defined perturbations.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving regulatory relationships at the level of individual cells, samples or interventions rather than population averages. FiberTron trains a compact model on one sample's Fiber-seq and nanopore RNA-seq data to predict base-level chromatin, methylation and transcript patterns and to test regulatory variant effects. In triple-negative breast cancer, a CRISPRi Perturb-seq framework combined with transcription-factor binding priors nominates CTCF, MYC and AP-1 family members as master regulators. CMC-VAE links genes and proteins across CITE-seq data, recovering regulatory structure while interventions refine perturbation predictions. scOnion scores cell-level concordance between paired gene expression and chromatin accessibility. GNEval provides a context-specific benchmark of gene associations from 11 single-cell foundation models against Gene Ontology and 14 Perturb-seq datasets. What is new is the use of single-sample multiomic long reads and standardized benchmarking of foundation-model gene networks; all results are preprint-level.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
